## 10. Testing Strategy

Frontend verification uses several layers.

### Static verification

`npm run typecheck`

Checks TypeScript compatibility.

### Unit testing

`npm test`

Runs the Vitest suite, including utility and component tests.

### Production compilation

`npm run build`

Confirms that the application can compile into a production build.

### Browser verification

Manual or automated browser checks validate navigation, interaction, layout and rendered content.

### Live integration verification

The frontend must also be tested against the deployed Render backend.

A passing mock-backed test does not establish that live API integration is working.

